// B1-v2 — canonical service key: <namespace>.<service>
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS
// Namespace arrives on spans under two MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE attributes:
//   * istio-mesh spans -> k8s.namespace.name  (service.name is already "<service>.<namespace>")
//   * app-SDK   spans -> service.namespace    (service.name is BARE, e.g. "frontend")
//
// Consequences measured over the R1-P1-collector window 2026-07-22T15:58:43Z -> 17:59:21Z
// (18,499,537 benchmark-tagged spans):
//
//   1. COLLISION. Bare "frontend" merges TWO different applications into one service
//      identity: hipster-shop 3,294,973 + otel-demo 892,424 = 4,187,397 spans (22.6% of
//      the run). Any per-service readout on service.name alone blends the two apps.
//      "frontend" is the only colliding name, but it is the single largest bucket.
//   2. SPLIT. The same workload appears twice - once as mesh "frontend.hipster-shop"
//      and once as app-SDK "frontend" - so its true volume is never seen in one place.
//
// This expression normalises BOTH paths to one key and fixes both problems at read time,
// with no change to the running telemetry config (so it is safe to apply retroactively to
// runs already banked, and it keeps the engine as the only variable across arms - see
// RUN-REGISTER.md self-check).
//
// VERIFIED: hipster-shop.frontend = 6,591,068 = 3,296,095 (mesh) + 3,294,973 (app-SDK).
//           otel-demo.frontend    = 1,390,604 =   498,180 (mesh) +   892,424 (app-SDK).
//
// CORRECTION (2026-07-23) - this file previously derived the namespace as
// `coalesce(service.namespace, k8s.namespace.name)` and carried a caveat warning not to use
// the result as an engine-comparison dimension. The caveat is gone because the DEPENDENCY is
// gone. k8s.namespace.name is written by the k8sattributes processor, i.e. by the ENGINE
// UNDER TEST, and a key that depends on engine enrichment can manufacture an engine
// difference that is not real. Istio already encodes the namespace in service.name as
// "<service>.<namespace>", and Istio config is frozen and identical across all three arms,
// so parsing it there gives the SAME coverage (95.07%) using only attributes written
// UPSTREAM of the engine:
//     service.namespace  <- the application's OTel SDK
//     service.name       <- the app SDK, or Istio's own naming convention
//     telemetry.sdk.name <- the emitting SDK/proxy
// The key is therefore safe as a comparison dimension, not only for drill-down.
// Verified identical row-for-row against the previous k8s.namespace.name form on R1-P1.
//
// KNOWN GAP: ~912,130 spans (4.9%) carry NEITHER attribute - almost all of them
// hipster-shop currencyservice app-SDK spans, which never set service.namespace. They
// surface as "<unattributed>.<service>" rather than being silently folded into a real
// namespace, so the gap stays visible instead of reading as a clean result.

fetch spans
| filter k8s.cluster.name == "${CLUSTER_NAME}" and isNotNull(benchmark.engine)
| fieldsAdd svc_parts = splitString(service.name, ".")
// namespace: app SDK first, then Istio's "<service>.<namespace>" convention
| fieldsAdd app = coalesce(service.namespace, svc_parts[1], "<unattributed>")
// service: strip Istio's namespace suffix so mesh and app-SDK spans land on ONE key
| fieldsAdd svc = coalesce(svc_parts[0], service.name)
| fieldsAdd service_key = concat(app, ".", svc)
// ingest path, derived independently of benchmark.telemetry_source so a dropped stamp
// cannot silently rewrite the split (dashboard defect 2). NB "envoy" alone is NOT enough:
// otel-demo's own frontend-proxy emits 422,380 Envoy spans that are not mesh sidecar
// spans - the dotted Istio service name is what separates them.
| fieldsAdd ingest = if(telemetry.sdk.name == "envoy" and isNotNull(svc_parts[1]), "istio-mesh", else: "app-sdk")
| summarize spans = count(), by:{ engine = benchmark.engine, service_key, ingest }
| sort spans desc
